# Core Workflow (LABOTEC Órdenes de Servicio)

> This is the stack-agnostic stub. If you installed a stack pack, it replaces this file
> with toolchain-specific guidance. Otherwise, the fill-pass should complete it.

## Toolchain

- **npm** + lockfile en la raíz (`package-lock.json`). No yarn / pnpm.
- Node **>=20** (Netlify `NODE_VERSION = "20"`).
- App en el workspace `labotec`. Comandos siempre desde la raíz (`npm run dev` / `build` / `preview`).

## Run / develop

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Install | `npm install` (raíz) |
| Run | `npm run dev` → Vite en `http://localhost:5173/` |
| Build | `npm run build` → `labotec/dist` |
| Preview | `npm run preview` |
| Lint / test | **No hay** script de lint ni test runner |
| Commit | Solo si el usuario lo pide; ver [git-workflow.mdc](git-workflow.mdc) |

## Verification

**No hay test runner automatizado** (ni Jest, ni Vitest, ni Playwright en `package.json`). Antes de review: `npm run build` y, si el cambio es UI, ejercitar el flujo en el browser (`npm run dev`). Un build verde no prueba persistencia ni RLS.

## Safety

- **Never add or commit secrets** — `.env*`, keystores, tokens. Only `*.example` templates are tracked.
- **Keep changes scoped**; avoid drive-by refactors unless required for the task.

